## Summary

Shipped a production-polished native Apple (SwiftUI) parity of `InfoTile.tsx` at `apps/apple/TeslaSync/feature-views/InfoTile.*` — committed as `5eebe3d2f`.

**Implementation** (6 files, CommandTile multi-file convention):
- `InfoTile.swift` — the `View` + convenience init + once-only `view.opened`.
- `InfoTile.Model.swift` — `InfoTileValue` (.text/.number/.bool with the web's boolean→"Yes"/"No" ternary), `InfoTileValueColor` tint mapped to semantic tokens (emerald→success, amber→warning, rose→danger, muted, primary…), accessibility builders, P1/S11 telemetry seam, P1/S10 i18n facade, `@Observable` model.
- `InfoTile.Views.swift` — `TSGlassPanel` (web GlassPanel `p-4`), muted icon+label row, tinted truncating value (`text-lg font-semibold`→Font.TS.section), optional sub; one combined VoiceOver element; `.help()` = web `title`.
- `InfoTile.Previews.swift` (8 previews, every branch), `InfoTile.Tests.swift` (14 tests), `InfoTile.strings`.

**Parity decisions:** pure presentational leaf → no data binding (matches source); boolean/blank words routed through the i18n facade (no English literals); blank value → em-dash so the tile is never empty. Data-lifecycle states (loading/error/stale/offline) are documented N/A — the web source has zero data layer.

